-- title:
--   Tensor product over a monogenic base as a quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $Z_0$ be a commutative ring, $V$ a commutative $Z_0$-algebra, and $\varpi \in V$ an element with $Z_0[\varpi] = V$, i.e. the $Z_0$-subalgebra generated by $\{\varpi\}$ is all of $V$. Let $A$ and $C$ be commutative rings that are simultaneously $Z_0$-algebras and $V$-algebras, with the two structures compatible (scalar-tower hypotheses over $Z_0 \to V \to A$ and $Z_0 \to V \to C$). Suppose $\mu \in A$ and $w \in C$ are elements whose images of $\varpi$ are given by $\varpi \cdot 1_A = 1 - \mu$ and $\varpi \cdot 1_C = 1 - w$ (equalities of $\mathrm{algebraMap}$ values). The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : (A \otimes_{Z_0} C)\big/\big(\mu \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes w\big) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; C \otimes_V A,$$
--   the quotient being by the ideal generated by the single element $\mu \otimes_{Z_0} 1 - 1 \otimes_{Z_0} w$, such that $e$ sends the class of $a \otimes_{Z_0} c$ to $c \otimes_V a$ for all $a \in A$, $c \in C$. Thus the isomorphism is specified on the images of pure tensors, with the two factors interchanged.
--
--   This is the standard base-change presentation of a tensor product over a monogenic base: passing from $\otimes_{Z_0}$ to $\otimes_V$ imposes exactly the one relation identifying the two images of the algebra generator $\varpi$. It is used to identify a branch algebra $(A \otimes C)/(\mu \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes w)$ occurring in the local analysis of completions of modular curves at cusps and in the ramification computations for full-level and $\Gamma_0$-level structures.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_TensorProduct_nonempty_ringEquiv_quotient_span_tmul_sub_tmul_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top.lean

